course: dictionary
lesson: 9545
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. Context, the words around a word, shows you which meaning fits. «Climb only on a steady step stool, never on a chair with wheels.» Here a stool is something you stand on to reach high places, not just something to sit on.
explain: A stool is a seat with legs but no back and usually no arms, like a bar stool at a kitchen counter. A footstool is a low stool for resting your feet. To check your meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Stool has a third meaning in medicine. Doctors and nurses use it as a polite word for poo when they check your health. The words around it, like doctor or health, tell you that is the meaning.
explain: Safety comes first. Use only a steady stool, with an adult nearby, and never a wobbly stool or a chair with wheels. When you meet a word with more than one meaning, ask yourself: which meaning fits here?
fact: A stool is a seat with legs but no back and usually no arms.
fact: A footstool is a low stool for resting your feet, or for standing on to reach something high.
fact: In medicine, «stool» is a polite word for poo, used by doctors and nurses.
fact: Phrases with stool include bar stool, piano stool, step stool and three-legged stool.
fact: Only climb on a steady step stool with an adult nearby. Never use a wobbly stool or a swivel chair.
exercise: What is a stool? | *A seat with legs but no back and usually no arms | A chair with wheels | A cupboard shelf | A low table for drinks
exercise: «Climb only on a steady step stool, never on a chair with wheels.» What is a step stool used for? | To hide under | To play the piano | To sit at a bar | *To reach high places safely
exercise: A doctor asks, «How is your stool?» What does stool mean here? | A seat for a bar | *Poo, a polite medical word | A footstool for resting your feet | A piano seat
test: «Never climb on a wobbly stool or a chair with wheels.» What should you use instead to reach a high cupboard? | A wheeled chair | *A steady step stool, with an adult nearby | A swivel chair | The counter edge
test: Which meaning of stool fits in «The footstool was under her feet»? | Poo, a polite medical word | A seat with a back and arms | *A low stool for resting your feet | A tall stool at a lab bench
exam: Jayden reads, «Doctors say stool when they check health.» What does stool mean here? | A step to reach a high shelf | *A polite word for poo | A seat with wheels | A bar stool at a counter
